A65. This keeps your poor old bones warm. ~ FLESH
A67. Ham preserver. ~ NOAH
A68. Fisherman. ~ LIAR
A69. Given Texas to remember Mexicans by. ~ ALAMO
A70. To smoke persistently. ~ CURE
A71. A foot behind. ~ LAME
A72. Old-fashioned Rumba or what to use to make woppie. ~ TARANTELLA

D1. Russian exports. ~ REDS
D2. A circle that's been sat on. ~ OVAL
D3. French author. ~ LOTI
D4. You can get a raise out of this, but Dora thinks it's just another Hebrew. ~ LEAVEN
D5. Quiet like a drunken sailor. ~ ROARING
D6. Shot in the body. ~ OLD
D7. What 1930 was. ~ YEAR
D8. Barred. ~ CAGED
D9. You'll get mad at this one (poss.). ~ ENEMYS
D10. Brings out the old smile. ~ GLADDENS
D11. This was in a hot spot before it came to table. ~ ROTI
D12. Bitter stuff to take. ~ ALOE
D13. Murphy in Haiti (plur.). ~ YAMS
D21. Weird lake. ~ ERIE
D23. Don't let this slip away if you get it. ~ EEL
